  {"id":321690,"slug":"stenotus-binotatus","sci":"Stenotus binotatus","common":"Two-spotted Grass Bug","family":"Miridae","obs":341,"regions":["central-cascades","gorge","olympics"],"months":[6,7],"photos":[{"id":1508166,"ext":"jpg","by":"Steve Kerr","lic":"CC BY"},{"id":501526176,"ext":"jpeg","by":"Mike Quinn, San Marcos","lic":"CC BY-NC"},{"id":29935478,"ext":"jpg","by":"Possums' End","lic":"CC BY"},{"id":107373577,"ext":"jpeg","by":"Steve King","lic":"CC BY-NC"},{"id":253399600,"ext":"jpg","by":"Gábor Keresztes","lic":"CC BY-NC"}],"wiki":"Stenotus binotatus","summary":"Stenotus binotatus is a species of plant bug, originally from Europe, but now also established across North America and New Zealand. It is 6–7 mm (0.24–0.28 in) long, yellowish, with darker markings on the pronotum and forewings. It feeds on various grasses, and can be a pest of crops such as wheat."},
